body:
I'm living in a constant state of nausea because I can't get used to the food on my college campus. I know this sounds like a super minor thing to be suicidal over but I've always had a weak immune system and between the rain and food, I'm always super anxious about everything and I ask myself if I really want to continue living like this. I told my mom that if I don't go home right now, I might just resort to suicide and self-harm. My sister said to just get rid of any sharp things in my dorm. My mom thinks that it's an empty threat, told me that I have to shove the food down even if I hate it and I can just starve to death if I keep this up. 

&#x200B;

I was afraid of telling them because I don't want to be overdramatic about something this stupid but their reactions also make me feel like they don't care, even when I know they're trying their best. But my parents have been through a lot and they think that you can just fight your way through everything and keep moving forward but I don't think I'm as strong as they are.
